  "remaining_gaps": [
    "RF per-node/feature histogram must fit 2048 shared bin slots; every selected row is still visited. Large row counts may regress despite fitting scratch.",
    "ET A admits raw-value nodes with at most 128 rows, one row per lane in a portable 128-thread block, and at most the existing 32 supported classes. Larger nodes and range-only rescue surveys retain B. This bounds per-thread work and shared state; it is not a reduced dataset recipe.",
    "Existing optional ET quantile-code regression retains B because its snapped threshold contract is distinct from raw-value range fusion. Weighted ET objectives remain a pre-existing unsupported public/native boundary. Missing/NaN refusal, bootstrap multiplicities and estimator settings are unchanged.",
    "The common setup, empty-cell conversion and canonical feature reducer remain separate launches. Small-node range and statistic row scans are skipped by those incumbent passes; the fused block forms statistics in shared memory and writes its final candidate. No workload, identity, quality or timing execution establishes a benefit."
  ],
  "numerical_contract": "S: unchanged feature sampling and key_for(seed,tree,node,feature), draw_threshold_device FTZ/FMA/max guard, exact integer class/label sums, regression_key and classification rational key, objective helpers and final split comparator. T14 combinations call the existing shared V1 MSE helper.",
  "et_source_call_path": "search_batch_enqueue or search_batch_regression_enqueue -> _enqueue_raw_range[FUSED_SMALL=True] reserves bounded nodes -> incumbent conversion seeds their invalid candidates -> _enqueue_small_node_splits -> small_node_raw_split_kernel -> unchanged split_reduce_kernel -> pack_splits -> existing stable partition/device frontier; range and draw outputs remain available to tracing.",
  "no_difference_notes": [
    "T06 caching continues on separately scored large ET nodes. T05 consumes each fused feature's parent terms once and therefore bypasses the separate multi-feature cache for those nodes; the same entropy statements remain.",
    "Host has no new device scheduling; the unchanged host exact objective graph remains the S counterpart. Runtime reach on any vendor is unverified."
  ],
